"bytes":232},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/m6120a3f.gif","alt":"The figure shows total state tobacco-related revenues and state and federal tobacco control appropriations compared with CDC Best Practices for Comprehensive Tobacco Control recommendations for tobacco control funding in the United States, during 1998-2010. From 1998 to 2010, the average state cigarette excise tax among all states and the District of Columbia increased from $0.39 to $1.44 per pack, resulting in a doubling of annual state excise tax revenues from $7.4 billion to $16.5 billion. In 2010, the excise tax ranged from $0.17 per pack in Missouri to $4.35 per pack in New York. During 1998-2010, annual settlement revenues increased from $1.4 billion in 1998, peaked at $9.3 billion in 2002, declined to $7.5 billion in 2003, and remained level to $7.4 billion in 2010.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":608,"renderedHeight":314,"naturalWidth":608,"naturalHeight":314,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 783 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":25497},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_out.png","alt":"External Web Site Icon","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":10,"renderedHeight":10,"naturalWidth":10,"naturalHeight":10,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":232},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_pdf.gif","alt":"Adobe PDF file","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":16,"renderedHeight":16,"naturalWidth":16,"naturalHeight":16,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":6058},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_wor